Based on the work of the OpenGOAL team

This editor is built on the work of the OpenGOAL team
(https://github.com/open-goal/jak-project):

- its extractor, ogle-extract, is made of the data readers of OpenGOAL's
  decompiler and level extractor, reduced and adapted (extractor/opengoal/,
  under OpenGOAL's ISC license: extractor/opengoal/LICENSE);
- the game data it comes with (data/<game>/game-data.json) is generated by
  tools/gen_game_data.py from OpenGOAL's decompiled game code;
- what it knows of the games' formats comes from their research.

This is an independent project. It is not affiliated with the OpenGOAL team,
nor endorsed or supported by it. It reuses OpenGOAL's license, the ISC license
above, and keeps the OpenGOAL team's copyright on what comes from their work.

Jak and Daxter, Jak II and Jak 3 belong to Sony Interactive Entertainment and
were developed by Naughty Dog. No data of the games comes with this project:
the levels are extracted from the user's own copy of a game. The screenshots
of docs/captures show levels of Jak II extracted that way.
